      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry, I wasn\u0027t clear the last time round. The concern with just concatenating for the HMAC input is that the MAC wouldn\u0027t detect changes where the attacker moves bytes out of pub and into ciphertext and vice versa. So the HMAC input is \"publicSECRET\" both for pub\u003d\"public\", cipher_text\u003d\"SECRET\" *and* also pub\u003d\"publicSECRET\", chiper_text\u003d\"\".\n\nI doubt this can be exploited in practice, but it\u0027s best to avoid this. Can be done easily by including the length field in the HMAC input before the actual data:\n\nHASH_update(\u0026hmac.hash, \u0026pub_len, sizeof(pub_len));\n\n(same for cipher_text_len).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 80,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 81,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "4e5f2bec5593a226950393e0b9b5efa3677eaf73",
