      "writtenOn": "2018-03-23T13:10:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hm, should we perhaps move this after hmac? I guess it comes down to the question on what should be done first: Version check or HMAC verification. My gut feeling is that we should do HMAC first, but we need to know the struct size for that. Also, you\u0027ll want the version number HMAC-protected, but at the same time you don\u0027t want to reach into the public data before it\u0027s been HMAC-checked.\n\nMaybe the best thing to do here would just be to put a separate version field here (and keep the one in leaf_public_data_t). The field here we wouldn\u0027t trust, but just use to detect struct layout?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 141,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 144,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "4e5f2bec5593a226950393e0b9b5efa3677eaf73",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
